Subject: [PATCH] core: carry dependency security fixes into the WASM build

The extension prover is built from this lockfile. Carry patched releases
into the core build without changing protocol code or manifests:
RUSTSEC-2026-0285 (rustls), RUSTSEC-2026-0258 (h2), and
RUSTSEC-2026-0204 (crossbeam-epoch). rustls-webpki follows rustls.
Also fix RUSTSEC-2026-0220 in ruint, used by attestation development tests.

Generated from TLSNotary 47aee45b53e06648c1b2ad3689b367b8c923fdec after
patches 0001 and 0002 with Cargo's resolver:

    cargo update -p rustls@0.23.40 --precise 0.23.45
    cargo update -p h2@0.4.13 --precise 0.4.16
    cargo update -p crossbeam-epoch@0.9.18 --precise 0.9.20
    cargo update -p ruint@1.18.0 --precise 1.20.0

Only those five existing package versions change. Cargo also adds ruint's
six ark-* 0.6 package records and resolves existing Windows-only edges to
already-locked windows-sys versions; retain those resolver-produced records
rather than editing package metadata by hand. The older TLS libraries used
by fixtures and development tests remain unsuppressed audit findings.

